concepts.distribution:
Codes belong to the portal, never to a version. This is already true in the domain: tokens are independent of snapshots, and publish, restore, pause and archive never revoke them. The UI states it as confidence, not explanation:
- the publish toast: "Printed codes keep working";
- the codes fact: "opens the live version (v5)".

Where codes live:
- The case's toolbar detail "QR + NFC · code v2 since 3 Sep" opens the Codes & print sheet.
- A first publish ends on the Publish & share page.
- Both show the code ledger: issued, replaced with a grace end, revoked with a reason, and print kits downloaded. This needs a new read of token and artifact history.

Print kits per composition (new):
- Formats: Table tent (A6 folded), Reception card (85×55), NFC card. Each is rendered in the property's composition (A, B or C), so print and screen share one design; Table Card is built for this.
- Rules built in:
  - the QR sits on a light plate with a 4-module quiet zone (today's PNG has 2);
  - error correction M;
  - dark modules on light, never inverted;
  - the short URL is printed as text;
  - honest CTA: "Rate your visit · private, about 30 seconds";
  - no Google logo, no stars;
  - the placement names a place, never a person;
  - NFC copy: "Hold the top of your phone to the card, then tap the link";
  - vector PDF with bleed and crop marks, and a true-size preview.
- A "Before you print" checklist: NTAG213/215/216, one URI record, locked after writing, on-metal tags where needed, and a test on an older phone in low light.

Replacing and revoking are overflow actions with a consequence sentence and a preview of the "no longer available" page:
- planned replacement (grace 1–90 days, default 30, both codes shown with the stop date);
- immediate security replacement;
- Revoke all (reason required).

Downloading again without rotating needs a security decision. My recommendation: for the beta, keep the address shown once, but make the print kit and the address download part of the issue moment (step 4 and the replacement flow). After the beta, decide whether an encrypted token may be retrieved by Account Admins and responsible managers, with every retrieval written to the ledger. Storing generated PDFs is the same as storing the token, so it is not a cheaper option.

Later:
- several named placements per portal ("Terrace tents ×12", "Reception card"), each with its own QR/NFC artifact. This is the path to per-placement scans and the QR vs NFC split, and needs a model change;
- per-link scheduling;
- scheduled publishing.

Test scans hit real tokens and would count as qualified scans. Product needs to decide whether authenticated admin sessions are excluded server-side. Until then, the checklist says test scans count.

concepts.brandGovernance:
Brand is a property-level decision, owned by the Account Admin and edited in one place: the Property brand studio (screen 10), reached from the rail footer. The studio's Look section and Property settings › Profile both link to it.

It holds:
- one composition per property: A Carved Stillness, B Folio or C Table Card;
- the three existing hex values: page background, text, brand colour;
- the display name, which is also the AI-reply business name, and the page says so;
- the property fallback wording per locale;
- link destination approvals.
Portal-local wording, links and threshold stay with the portal.

Composition is chosen by polarity:
- the studio recommends Carved Stillness when the derived accent reaches 3:1 on the dark stage, and Folio otherwise;
- Table Card is offered for restaurants, bars and loud brands;
- a composition that cannot work for the colours is disabled with its reason, never silently degraded.
Folio's night edition is a later per-portal option for evening placements. A per-portal composition override (Table Card for a hotel's pool bar) is a later Account Admin decision, not in the beta.

Colours have derived roles and are never free pickers. The derived-token engine computes and shows as facts:
- the accent at 3:1 for stars, rules and focus, and at 4.5:1 for small accent text;
- the idle star (text mixed 55% into the surface);
- a black or white button label.
A failing role gets a suggested fix ("Use #7A5C3E") with "Use suggestion", never raw ratios. The same check becomes a publish gate; today only text contrast is enforced. The SaaS-blue default #2563EB (and the #6366F1 renderer fallback) is replaced with the neutral hospitality default #1E1C1A / #F6F2EA / #7A5C3E, which lands on Folio.

Impact is always listed before and after saving:
- "Affects 7 portals: 5 live will wait for publishing, 2 drafts update now", with a detail listing each portal and its other pending changes.
- Saving writes the brand profile and fans out pending changes (the portal_pending_content_changes data already exists; a property-level read is new).
- Nothing live changes until each portal is published, individually or in the batch review.
- Unpublished changes on affected portals read "Brand change waiting".

Guest copy packs follow the same path. A new pack (v2) lands as "New guest wording available" in Unpublished changes, with a batch adopt.

A PM sees the brand studio read-only, with "Only an Account Admin can change the brand · Elena Petrova" and "Suggest a change" (a new notification request). Uploads stay blocked: logo and photo slots show the finished no-photo composition.

concepts.inboxConsistency:
1. Facts, controls and details wear different clothes.
   - Facts: Live · version 4, codes and health are 13px text with a glyph and no box.
   - Controls: Owners, Group and ⋯ are outline 32px buttons with chevrons, grouped in a ButtonGroup with the facts, like the inbox case toolbar.
   - Details: Draft · 3 changes, metric definitions and "What guests see" use a dotted underline and open popovers.
   - No pills, except the phone queue strip, which the inbox also uses.
   - The filled purple "Published" badge and the list swatch are retired.
2. Purple is interactive only. Health uses a neutral dot, or `triangle-alert` in #a45f00 plus words. Metric bars are #5b5d63 and lines #101115. Deltas carry a sign and words. The guest preview carries the property brand inside a device outline, and the admin never takes its colours.
3. Private is words, plus a dashed edge, plus amber. "Private notes" and "Average private rating" always carry the word private. The Private-note preview state keeps the guest's own treatment. The warn family is never used as a bare health signal.
4. The ledger. One Timeline per portal: 32px people indicators, 24px system indicators, a 2px connector, sentences in the form actor · verb · object · time, routine runs folded. It records publications, restores, health, codes, brand, managers and approvals. It replaces the read-only history card and a separate Share history.
5. One primary action per area, and guarantees live in tooltips and toasts:
   - list: New portal;
   - case dock: Review & publish, or Edit portal / Continue setup;
   - review: Publish version 5;
   - codes: Download print kit;
   - brand dock: Save brand, then Review & publish n;
   - Performance: none.
   "Printed codes keep working", "Try as guest records nothing" and "Google stays the same for every guest" are carried by the toast or a tooltip, never a standing paragraph.
6. Availability by exception. Healthy portals are quiet. An empty queue is one sentence naming the queue plus one action. Thin data gets a number with n where there is one, otherwise a sentence plus "Widen the range", never a dash. Provenance sits at the end in a details disclosure.
7. Modes, not pages. Search is a mode of the list header. Bulk selection is the list header in another state. Editing is a studio mode entered from the case and left with Esc, the way the composer is part of the case. Empty states name the queue.
8. The same geometry and contracts:
   - 224 rail, 400 list, 56 headers, 78px rows, 48px toolbar, radius-12 dock, 1078 desktop floor;
   - queue= and the other URL state, like ADR 0057;
   - the scope select pattern from #582;
   - j/k and the ? legend;
   - the metrics gate.

scores.strengths:
The most literal and disciplined use of the inbox language:
- the queue rail with a scope select (#582 pattern) and a server-side queue-count read, the getInboxQueueCounts mirror;
- fixed 78px rows with signals first;
- a case with a fact/control toolbar;
- attention lines, each naming who can fix it and one fix;
- a draft dock that is the composer dock's twin, with one primary;
- j/k and the ? legend;
- URL queue state per ADR 0057.

**Best domain accuracy on the history.**
- Restore keeps version 3 as version 3 with a new activation.
- Undo is correctly flagged as needing a rule change (target must be lower than active today).
- After a restore, the draft shows v4's content as not live, which is correct given the working-copy digest comparison.
- It states honestly that a non-verified Google link, including awaiting_refresh, blocks every publish at the property. update-portal requires state === 'verified'.
- Notification policy matches the actionable-reason list: no alert for refresh, plus a quiet 'back to normal'.

**Best build planning.**
- Every capability is classified A, B or C against the map.
- The phases are P1–P4, with P1 built mostly from A reads plus B1–B3.
- New commands are called out explicitly: a reviewed-digest guard on publish and 'Discard draft changes'.
- The most conservative security stance: keep shown-once for the beta, bind the kit to the issue and replace moments, and note that storing PDFs is equivalent to storing the token.

**Accessibility.** Accessible row names include the signals. Nothing is swipe-only, glyphs have sr-only counts, and 2.5.7 moves are provided.

**The strongest fairness proof and identity story.**
- After rating defaults to a 1★/5★ pair, with a dashed guide across both frames at the Google card's top edge.
- The Studio has no arrows or conditional rules, so it cannot read as a routing builder.
- Review includes a contact sheet of every guest state in EN and BG, with changed regions marked.

**Useful ideas for the other concepts:**
- the best comparison rule: percentages only when the prior period has 10 or more, otherwise absolute differences;
- a neutral default identity created at property setup, removing one Account-Admin-only publish blocker (flagged as a decision);
- 'Paste colours';
- 'Copy identity to…' across properties;
- an 'allowed alternate composition' as a concrete answer to the hotel pool-bar case;
- pinning the colour-engine version in snapshots, so derivation changes never shift live pages.

**Domain facts it gets right.**
- Restore semantics: 'Live · version 3 (restored)', a rollback activation, and the draft kept.
- Resume is a publish with checks.
- The identity impact review discloses other editors' pending work, with opt-outs for each row.
